                         FUNCTION MODIFICATIONS
                              DETAILS
================================================================================

DESTRUCTOR ADDED:
  PatronsCollection::~PatronsCollection()
  - Deallocates all dynamically allocated Patron objects
  - Prevents memory leaks

ADDPATRON() MODIFIED:
  Before: patronsList.emplace_back(first, last);  // Type error
  After:
    - Calculate next available ID
    - Allocate new Patron on heap
    - Push pointer to vector
    - Display confirmation with assigned ID

EDITPATRON() MODIFIED:
  Before: p->Edit();  // Non-existent method
  After:
    - Get patron reference
    - Display current name
    - Prompt for new name
    - Allow user to keep current value if blank
    - Update and confirm

DELETEPATRON() MODIFIED:
  Before: patronsList.erase() with lambda using GetID()
  After:
    - Find patron pointer using std::find
    - Delete allocated memory
    - Erase from vector
    - Display confirmation

PRINTALLPATRONS() MODIFIED:
  Before: Loop over auto& p; p.Print()
  After:
    - Changed to auto* p for pointer iteration
    - Check if collection is empty
    - Display formatted patron information
    - Show: Name | ID | Fines | Books

FINDPATRONBYID() MODIFIED:
  Before: return &p;  // Would return pointer to pointer
  After:
    - Return Patron* directly (not &Patron*)
    - Proper pointer semantics

FINDPATRONBYNAME() MODIFIED:
  Before: Concatenated GetFirstName() + GetLastName()
  After:
    - Uses getName() which returns full name
    - Trims input for comparison
    - Returns Patron* directly

PRINTPATRON() IMPLEMENTED:
  - New function implementation
  - Finds patron by name or ID
  - Displays detailed patron information

PAYFINE() IMPLEMENTED:
  - New function implementation
  - Handles fine payment processing
  - Updates patron fine balance
  - Provides user feedback

